Or even:

=A0=A0=A0 (4) mi ponse lo karce .i blabi
=A0=A0=A0 =A0 =A0 (sort of literally: "I own Car. Whites.")[1]
=A0=A0=A0 =A0 =A0 "I own a car. It is white."

While this is not entirely an example of {le} vs {lo}, it's still a very co=
mmon way to say it, and it shows that even this level of vagueness is appro=
